who had the most ill-fitting outfit on  miami vice and what was moira's most  outrageous ensemble on shit's creek here  are a few television costuming choices  that may have gone a little overboard  what's worse carrie bradshaw falling  flat on her face during her first ever  runway walk or her wardrobe during the  infamous tumble you be the judge in the  season 4 sex and the city episode the  real me carrie is invited to participate  in a charity fashion show alongside  heidi klum and former mayor ed koch both  of whom appear as themselves while she  was originally slated to wear a dolce  gabbana dress a last-minute change puts  carrie in a pair of bedazzled panties  needless to say she's not a fan of the  idea at first how can i make this clear  me no likey the idea of having one's  groin area literally sparkling with the  radiant reflections of diamonds in the  light is certainly a romantic notion but  that doesn't excuse it being paired with  carrie's puffed-up hairdo and  knee-length glam jacket sex in the city  was always one of the most  fashion-forward shows but this  particular getup was destined to be a  disaster still at least carrie was able  to stand up after her fall and finish  her runway walk without any other  incidents  as an fbi agent who spends most of his  time chasing cryptids fox mulder can't  be expected to stay up to date on  fashion trends even so the early days of  the x-files saddled the beleaguered  believer with some ridiculously  oversized trench coats the choice makes  practical sense since the show was shot  in chile vancouver for its first five  seasons but the sheer size of mulder's  jacket could be an x-file on its own  upon closer examination the jacket is  likely as large as it is in order to  accommodate another fashion faux pas  that hadn't quite been phased out by the  early 1990s the oversized shoulder pads  or mulder suit jacket between the pads  and david duchovny's already broad  shoulders it kinda makes sense that the  jacket needed to be absurdly huge with a  fashion sense like that it's no wonder  it took until season seven for mulder  and scully to finally share their first  official kiss  one of batman's most famous villains the  riddler quickly became a fan favorite on  the original 1960s batman series  starring adam west as the caped crusader  in the first and third seasons of the  show riddler is played by frank gorshin  who earned an emmy nomination for his  performance as the quizzical villain  however for the character's appearance  in season 2 jon aston was cast in the  role instead presumably because gorshin  was unavailable at the time while aston  best known as gomez from the addams  family does a decent enough job as the  riddler he doesn't fill out the  character's costume in quite the same  way gorshin was an extremely skinny man  one of the few actors who could  effectively wear a skintight leotard  without looking unintentionally silly  john astin while not overweight simply  didn't have a body type that was  flattered by such a costume decades  later when jim carrey took on the role  of the riddler in batman forever he wore  a skin-tight leotard costume that paid  tribute to frank gorshin's iconic outfit  thankfully carrie was just as skinny as  gorson so there was no unfortunate  curves on his version of the eccentric  enigma  in the final frontier there will be  unisex minidresses while his intentions  were noble series creator gene  roddenberry's idea of a starfleet  uniform designed for both men and women  ultimately proved to be something of a  misfire for the science fiction series  his reasoning was simple if women in  star trek can wear pants like the men  traditionally do then there should be a  skirt that men can wear too alas the  scant as it was called looked silly in  practice with its tiny sleeves making  its wearers look like uncomfortable  children the scant only made sporadic  appearances in the early days of the  next generation and was quickly phased  out with most of the crew members  transitioning to pants more recently the  animated series star trek lower decks  took a much deserved shot at the  ill-fitting outfit should we be in scans  for this nobody wears those anymore  don't overthink it perhaps if riker or  picard had given the scan a chance the  fashion of star trek would have gone  down a different path as it is however  this awkward minidress is just a  footnote in track history  oliver queen more commonly known as the  green arrow wears a green leather  ensemble that hides his identity while  providing a degree of protection from  physical blows for the most part his  costume is chic and functional allowing  the righteous vigilante to look cool  while fighting to save the city that he  loves unfortunately the version of his  outfit seen in season 4 of arrow doesn't  exactly hit the bull's eye most  glaringly this particular costume is  sleeveless while it does a good job of  showing off steven amell's big arms it  looks more like the wardrobe department  ran out of material during production  his long gloves and arm guards don't do  much to hide how silly the whole thing  looks at times queen's shoulders are  even covered by big rounded shoulder  pads which make him look more like a  ninja turtle than an emerald archer  finally the costume simply isn't green  enough but it was apparently supposed to  be since several scenes put a cheap cg  filter over the suit in an attempt to  make it pop fortunately this was all  fixed in season 5 ditching the bizarre  overlay and bringing sleeves back to the  costume  moira rose played by catherine o'hara in  the hit tv series shit's creek is the  walking definition of over the top not  an episode of the show goes by in which  she doesn't wear a bizarre costume and a  horrific wig to match throughout the  series her outfits run the gamut from  absolute nightmare to okay that's  actually pretty good for the grand  series finale in which moira serves as  the officiant for her son's wedding she  pulls out all the stops and dons the  worst or best outfit ever seen on the  show this particular getup is moira's  take on the pope complete with a long  gown and giant mitre her rig is  relatively normal by her standards  though its blonde locks do inexplicably  line the entire brim of the pope hat the  real cherries on top are the golden  gloves complete with several rings rings  over gloves may be the ultimate fashion  sin but that doesn't stop moira from  doing a fantastic job with the wedding  making for a touching final chapter to  the shit's creek saga  former the shield star michael chicklish  joined the cast of fox's batman origin  story gotham in its second season as  nathaniel barnes a no-nonsense  tough-as-nails cop with a checkered past  when he's infected by a drop of blood  from mad hatter's dead sister he becomes  something even nastier he becomes the  executioner an original villain created  for the show as the executioner barnes  murders criminals which inevitably puts  him into conflict with the more  ethically minded jim gordon he wears  green arrow style grease paint over his  eyes and adorns himself with armor that  looks like something a sinobyte from  hellraiser might wear the awkward armor  is provided to barnes by the court of  owls a secret society that has pulled  gotham strings for generations maybe  that's why they gave him a costume that  looks like it's from a straight to video  sequel to eyes wide shut  suel and mishki arch nemesis of elaine  bennis and heir to the old henry candy  bar fortune may have only appeared on  four episodes of seinfeld but she  certainly made a lasting impression in  her debut on season seven's the caddy  sue ellen refuses to wear a bra while  out in public prompting elaine to buy  one for her as a passive aggressive  birthday present sue ellen responds by  wearing the bra as a top on its own with  nothing but a blazer to cover it up this  unconventional outfit distracts jerry  and kramer while they're on the road  causing a car accident that leads to a  trial parodying the old j simpson case  when asked to put on the bra over her  leotard the garment doesn't fit and just  like johnny cochran famously said about  oj's bloody glove if it doesn't fit  you must acquit of course a bra is not  going to fit on over leotard a bra gotta  fit right up against a person's skin  like a glove  as a result sue ellen goes unpunished  for her crimes against fashion by the  end of the episode the idea of wearing a  bra as a top becomes a huge hit with the  public  decades before denis villeneuve turned  dune into a hollywood blockbuster the  sci-fi channel aired frank herbert's  doom a mini-series based on the  acclaimed 1965 novel produced on a  budget of 20 million dollars the  mini-series aired in 2000 and became a  huge hit for the network there is a wide  variety of factions within the world of  doom and the miniseries way of conveying  these disparate allegiances was to give  each group a different style of costume  often accentuated by distinct headwear  unfortunately these costumes can be more  than a little distracting today frank  herbert's dune is remembered mainly for  its wacky outfits particularly the hats  worn by characters like princess eurelin  but honestly nearly every character can  be described as fashion overkill  this whole list could consist of nothing  but entries from miami vice such was the  glorious audacity of the groundbreaking  series sense of style however the first  place honor has to go to actor timmy  cappello who appeared in season three's  theresa as the enforcer arzola this  gun-toting henchman wears a bizarrely  misshapen tank top that's so ghastly he  ends up taking it off partway through  the episode while he's set up as an  intimidating thug arzola is  unceremoniously killed when he runs into  traffic while trying to escape from  protagonist sunny crockett  across the four seasons of his comedy  central series nathan for you nathan  fielder made a career out of trying to  revitalize struggling businesses through  hilariously unconventional means his  ideas have ranged from abusing you break  it you buy it policies to selling a one  dollar tv guarded by a live alligator  all with varying degrees of success  however one of his more bizarre and  messy plans involved a plastic suit  filled with delicious chili in a season  4 episode filder meets with a chilly  shop owner whose dream is to sell his  food at a nearby hockey stadium  unfortunately the stadium isn't offering  contracts to outside vendors fielder's  plan to smuggle chile into the arena to  sell by hiding it in a custom-built  bodysuit after some rigorous testing and  a few redesigns the show's host dons the  covert chili dispenser and actually  manages to sneak it past security under  some plus-sized hockey merch believe it  or not the plan is relatively successful  as fielder is able to sell 16 bowls and  bring back a 20 profit whether or not it  was worth carrying 30 pounds of chili  around for over an hour is a different  story check out one of our newest videos  right here plus even more looper videos  about your favorite shows are coming  soon subscribe to our youtube channel  and hit the bell so you don't miss a  single one  you

